SUMMARY:TEDxBoston: Visions of the Next 250
LOCATION:Offsite: GBH Studios
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are on Waitlis
 t\nTime: 3 PM – 7 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events
 /190012\n\nFor 250 years\, Massachusetts has produced the ideas that shape
 d a nation: public education\, the telephone\, the first American node of 
 the World Wide Web. The next 250 begin now.\n\nAs part of the statewide Ou
 r America 250 initiative\, join us at GBH for a one-day gathering on what 
 comes next. Thirty speakers take the stage in interviews and talks\, mappi
 ng the forces that will define America's next chapter: artificial intellig
 ence\, the future of work\, energy and climate technology\, and the reinve
 ntion of education.\n\nA preview of featured speakers:\n\nAndrew Lau - CEO
  of Jellyfish\nJoseph Aoun - President of Northeastern University and auth
 or of Robot-Proof\nLibby Wayman - Partner at Breakthrough Energy Ventures\
 nNeil Thompson - Director of MIT FutureTech and Principal Investigator at 
 MIT's Initiative on the Digital Economy\n\nCurated and moderated by John W
 erner\, venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI columnist. Every
  talk is recorded as a living time capsule\, a message to the generations 
 who will open it on the road to America's 500th.\n\nPlease look forward to
  additional details regarding related Programming hosted at The 'Quin on J
 une 22nd. More information to follow.\n\n*This event is complimentary and 
 reserved for members\, plus one guest.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/190012
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
